WHAT THESE TERMS COVER
======================

They cover the GlucoCube software in this repository. They do not cover the
following, each of which carries its own terms and is not the licensor's to
place under these.

  The bundled fonts — glucocube/fonts/

      JetBrains Mono (Copyright 2020 The JetBrains Mono Project Authors) and
      Space Grotesk (Copyright 2020 The Space Grotesk Project Authors) are
      licensed solely under the SIL Open Font License 1.1, whose text sits
      beside them in OFL-JetBrainsMono.txt and OFL-SpaceGrotesk.txt. That
      license requires the fonts to be distributed entirely under it and
      under no other license, so nothing here reaches them: your rights in
      the fonts, including using them commercially, are unaffected by
      anything below.

  The enclosure — enclosure/

      Designed by Sarah Sabanis and licensed separately under the Creative
      Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 International
      License. See enclosure/LICENSE.

  The SD card image

      A GlucoCube image is Raspberry Pi OS, which is Debian: hundreds of
      packages under the GPL, the LGPL and various permissive licenses,
      plus redistributable Raspberry Pi firmware. Each keeps its own terms,
      and these terms reach only the GlucoCube layer on top of them — no
      noncommercial restriction is or could be imposed on any of it.
      Sources for the Debian components are published at
      https://sources.debian.org, and for the Raspberry Pi components by
      Raspberry Pi Ltd.

Names used to describe what GlucoCube talks to — Raspberry Pi, Nightscout,
Trio, Tidepool, twiist, Loop, OpenAPS — belong to their respective owners
and are used only to say what works with what. The glucose forecast
reimplements the exponential insulin-activity model from oref0
(https://github.com/openaps/oref0) in Python, with thanks.


NOT A MEDICAL DEVICE
====================

GlucoCube is a convenience display. It is not a medical device. It has not
been reviewed or approved by any regulator, and it must not be used to make
treatment decisions. Its forecasts are estimates — including the ones that
come from the pump or AID system itself. It raises no alarms and must not
be relied upon for any. Use the CGM's own application and alerts for
anything that matters.

The software is provided as is and without warranty of any kind, as set out
under "No Liability" below.


